  "question": {
    "text": "Two small spheres each of mass <math><mi>m</mi></math> and charge <math><mi>q</mi></math> are tied from the same rigid support with the help of silk threads of length <math><mi>L</mi></math>. They make angle <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math> with the vertical as shown in the figure. If length <math><mi>L</mi></math> is decreased, then angle <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">θ</mi></math> with the vertical&nbsp;<br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0135_e7bfed235d6b.png\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 191px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "increases",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "decreases",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "unaffected",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "cannot say",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "When length is decreased, distance between two charges decreases and so, the force of repulsion increases. So for equilibrium,&nbsp;<math> <mi>θ</mi> </math> also increases."
  }
